#' @title K-means Clustering on Principal Components with Comprehensive Diagnostics
#'
#' @description
#' Runs k-means clustering over a user-defined range of `k` values on a low-dimensional
#' embedding (e.g., PCA). For each `k`, computes:
#' - Within-cluster sum of squares (WCSS)
#' - Average silhouette width (if distance matrix is feasible)
#' - Calinski-Harabasz index
#' - Davies-Bouldin index
#'
#' Automatically selects the **optimal `k`** using a robust hierarchy:
#' 1. **Maximize silhouette** → best separation
#' 2. **Tie-break with CH index** → cluster compactness
#' 3. **Fallback to WCSS elbow** → if internal indices fail
#'
#' Outputs:
#' - Per-k silhouette plots
#' - Elbow & metrics panel
#' - Final cluster assignments (CSV)
#' - Full reproducibility: per-k cluster CSVs
#'
#' @param PC Numeric matrix of principal components (samples x PCs). Row names = sample IDs.
#' @param outdir Output directory. Created if missing.
#' @param k_grid Integer vector of `k` values to test (e.g., `2:8`).
#' @param seed Random seed for `kmeans` reproducibility.
#' @param sample_is_tcga Logical vector (length = nrow(PC)) indicating TCGA samples.
#'                       Used for stratified reporting. Optional.
#' @param V_adj Optional normalized expression matrix (genes x samples).
#'              Used for diagnostic checks (variance, matching).
#'
#' @return Invisible list:
#' \item{best_k}{Optimal number of clusters}
#' \item{res_list}{List of k-means objects and silhouette per `k`}
#' \item{metrics}{Data frame of WCSS, Silhouette, CH, DB}
#' \item{clusters}{Final cluster factor (C1, C2, ...)}
#' \item{cluster_df}{Tibble with sample, dataset, cluster}
#'
#' @export